Start a tool, workflow, or pipeline run (`run <KIND> <NAME>`), or run one pipeline on one input

Usage: thorctl run <tool|workflow|pipeline> <NAME> [OPTIONS]
       thorctl run <PIPELINE> <SHA256_OR_REPO> [OPTIONS]

Commands:
  tool      Run a tool instance, or a tool's latest version (the same as `thorctl tools run`)
  workflow  Run a workflow instance, or a workflow's latest (the same as `thorctl workflows run`)
  pipeline  Run a pipeline (legacy: the same as `thorctl pipelines run`; prefer tools and workflows)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  <PIPELINE>        The pipeline to run
  <SHA256_OR_REPO>  The sample SHA256 or repo to run the pipeline on

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Older form:
      --group <GROUP>    The group that the pipeline is in (required if a pipeline with the same
                         name exists in another group)
  -s, --sla <SLA>        How many seconds allowed to wait before starting the job [default: 1]
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>  The path to save the results to [default: `<SHA256/REPO>_<PIPELINE>`]

Older form: thorctl run <PIPELINE> <SHA256|REPO> [--group <GROUP>] [--sla <SECONDS>] [--output
<PATH>] creates one reaction and prints each stage's output as it runs.

For many inputs use `--one-per-input` (one run per file or repo, tagged with a shared `--batch`
name); `thorctl runs get --batch <NAME>` lists a batch and `thorctl runs cancel --batch <NAME>`
cancels it.
